            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for a canopy, then the Urdu for a night's shelter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: خراب",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "خراب — kharāb — \"out of order; bad\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کمرے کا پنکھا خراب ہے۔ kamre kā pankhā kharāb hai. The fan in the room isn't working."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic kharāb, \"ruin, desolation\"; in Urdu a broken fan, spoilt food and bad weather are all خراب."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
